Z||000003||Shaun41178||11-03-1999||02:32 AM||||RS Motorsports now has a supercharger kit for the v6.  Dyno numbers and charts are up on their webpage.  200 hp is reported at the wheels with 9 psi of boost which is around 220 in a manual tranny at the crank.  an auto tranny would probably have about 190 at the wheels.  But still 220 crank hp is a good amount and the torque has to be unbelieveable down low.<P>Pics of the kit are also up on the website.  i suggest everyone check it out.  The address is  <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A> <BR>and then go to engine & performance.<P>For $2800 I think it is a darn good deal.  Since the kit is brand new reliability of the kit might be in question but I am sure they will warranty the kit.  <P>For those of you that have your 3.2's already by adding this kit will probably give around 330 hp or so at the crank.  330 hp in a 2800 pound car.  That should be good for high 12's easy in the qtr and 0-60 times of sub 5 seconds traction limited of course.  Get fat tires for sure.  i think I might get this kit after my 3.2 is done.  I am building my engine for forced induction of one kind or another so I am sure I can up the boost with no problems but with 9 psi I expect power to be around 350 hp with my setup.  Perhaps a shot of funny fumes too just for good measure although I bet I will never need it on the street as almost no car will hang from a stop or slow roll.  <P>Check it out guys.  I think this kit is a good substitute for a turbo and cheaper too.<P>Shaun<BR>85 GT with nitrous <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A> <BR>best e.t. to date: 14.1 @ 89 mph||||reg||1
